    "chunk_text": "4.3 section 15.4 of the Code of Electoral Regulations is hereby amended by the addition therefor of the following paragraph. The nomination paper should be prepared in 02 copies. Such nomination paper should conform to the form \u201ca\u201d of the Schedule four of this Code of Electoral Regulations and should have been duly completed and placed signature.\n\n(a) National Identity Card (b) Valid Driving License (c) Valid Passport (d) Pensioners\u2019 Identity Card issued by the Director of Pensions (e) Elders\u2019 Identity Card issued by the Divisional Secretary (f) A valid Identity Card issued to the monks / priests by Ministry of Religious Affairs or a State Department in charge of Religious Affairs.\n\n5.2 section 16.2of the Code of Electoral Regulations is hereby amended by the addition therefor of the following paragraph. After examining a nomination paper handed over, it should be rejected only during the period from 10.00 a.m. to 10.15 a.m. only at the occasions under mentioned.\n\n5.3 By the addition of the following new section as 16.2 (III) after 16.2 (II).\n\n(III) At an instance where one of three persons of candidate or proposer or seconder has not handed over the nomination paper.\n\nAmendment of sections16.1 and 16.2 of the Code of Regulations\n\nAddition of sub section 16.2 (iii) of the Code of Regulations\n\n4 A IV(A) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.07.12 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 12.07.2019\n\nAmendment of sections16.3, 16.4 and 16.5 of the Code of Regulations"
